& [Problem]
  + EVO-X2 proves an older bounded Needle2-to-Cantor-to-llama.cpp attention route but does not yet prove that the current published Cantor build can be installed identified replayed or used as a governed build-work coordinator on that host
  + historical routing evidence is not evidence of current binary compatibility self-work ability product readiness semantic quality or autonomous operation
  + copying the current build into a historical runtime root would erase the distinction between preserved evidence and a new experiment

& [Objective]
  + establish EVO-X2 as an isolated current-build Cantor pilot host without modifying the historical deployment
  + transfer an exact content-addressed subset of current published release executables and their provider-free retained evidence into a new versioned root
  + verify local and remote byte counts and SHA256 before and after every executable replay
  + use the current independent A8 evidence verifier as the first current-build execution because it proves a complete published dependency chain without provider access
  + if and only if the current cantor query executable is byte-compatible with copied public historical environment/query fixtures, run one isolated read-only query replay against those copies
  + measure wall duration process exit typed outcome and artifact identity while making no claim about universal performance
  + produce a machine-readable deployment and experiment receipt that a separate verifier can check locally after retrieval

& [ArtifactSelection]
  + pin the exact source commit and canonical remote ref before packaging
  + select the smallest executable set needed for current identity replay and measurement: current cantor query runtime and current A8 independent evidence verifier
  + select only the exact retained provider-free A8 evidence directory required by that verifier and two copied public historical query fixtures if compatibility replay is admitted
  + do not transfer target directories dependency caches source history credentials private permit material models toolchains or unrelated evidence
  + every selected file is enumerated by normalized relative path byte count and lowercase SHA256 in a canonical deployment manifest

& [RemoteRootAndInstallation]
  + final root is C:/AI/services/cantor-current-pilot-48479932 and staging is a unique sibling beneath C:/AI/services
  + refuse if final root already exists with any unrecognized bytes; never merge overwrite or repair in place
  + create staging transfer exact files verify the manifest and atomically rename staging to final only after all identities match
  + installation creates no service scheduled task environment-variable change registry entry PATH entry firewall rule port listener persistent process or automatic startup
  + historical Cantor Needle2 SOP-agent llama.cpp model and configuration paths are read-only dependencies or observations and never installation targets

& [ExperimentCircuit]
  + phase E0 audits host identity free space existing protected roots provider process and final-root absence without mutation
  + phase E1 composes the exact local package manifest from published current artifacts and verifies all local identities
  + phase E2 installs the immutable pilot root through a unique staging directory and verifies exact remote membership identities ACL observation and no protected-root drift
  + phase E3 runs the A8 independent evidence verifier twice in fresh processes and requires byte-identical canonical success records with exit zero
  + phase E4 may run current cantor once against copied public historical fixtures only after an explicit compatibility preflight proves the command contract and fixture hashes; incompatibility is a typed skipped result rather than permission to alter fixtures
  + phase E5 retrieves the bounded receipt, independently verifies it against the local manifest, re-audits protected roots and provider process identity, and leaves no pilot process running
  + a later separately governed phase may give Cantor a bounded build-planning or physical build contract; this P0 does not let a model edit compile commit push or self-update the repository

& [PerformanceMeasures]
  + report package file count and bytes install duration verifier duration per replay query duration when admitted exit status result bytes and deterministic equality
  + report host CPU GPU memory and storage only as observational context and do not infer utilization or throughput without a measured counter
  + compare the current replay to itself and to the preserved historical route baseline only by explicitly common measures; response-byte reduction is not inference-speed improvement
  + successful evidence verification proves executable portability and contract replay, not generative quality or autonomous engineering productivity

& [EffectBoundary]
  + authorized effects are SSH observation creation of one versioned staging/final pilot root exact file transfer executable replay receipt write and receipt retrieval
  + allowed executable inputs are content-pinned public provider-free evidence and content-pinned copied public fixtures
  + no external network model download package install Rust build provider fallback credential lookup secret echo private permit activation Git mutation source write service restart or policy change
  + no executable receives a path outside the new pilot root except read-only operating-system runtime dependencies
  + do not stop restart reconfigure or replace llama.cpp Needle2 SOP-agent or the historical Cantor attention adapter

& [ThreatsAndRefusals]
  + refuse wrong SSH host identity wrong source commit changed origin equality insufficient space unsafe path grammar final-root collision staging collision symlink reparse point nonregular file extra file missing file digest mismatch or unlisted executable
  + refuse manifest traversal absolute relative parent path duplicate case-folded path inconsistent byte count wrong digest mutable protected-root identity provider PID or command-line drift and any attempted endpoint exposure
  + rejected path or secret-shaped values are summarized by field and class without echoing sensitive contents
  + if transfer or verification fails preserve a bounded failure receipt and remove only the exact newly created staging root after resolving and checking its absolute path; never recursively remove the final root or a computed broad parent

& [EvidenceAndVerification]
  + retain canonical package manifest local preflight remote install receipt two independent verifier outputs optional query result and final audit as exact files under a new experiment evidence directory
  + the deployment script and independent verifier use closed path grammar bounded file count bounded aggregate bytes exact ordered membership and SHA256 before semantic parsing
  + tests cover safe manifest valid replay wrong commit root collision missing extra changed traversal absolute duplicate reparse and post-execution drift cases without contacting EVO-X2
  + one explicitly invoked live test may contact only SSH alias evo-x2 and the loopback provider observation; default tests remain provider-free and host-free
  + source SJS signature plan matrix phase lock and verification scripts precede the live installation

& [Acceptance]
  + source commit and SJS formation are published with direct local/remote equality before new remote bytes are created
  + current executable and evidence bytes are pinned to published Git lineage and match on EVO-X2 before and after execution
  + two A8 evidence replays pass independently with byte-identical typed results and no provider requests
  + optional query replay is either compatibly passed or truthfully skipped with a bounded reason; it is never coerced by changing the historical contract
  + protected deployments and provider process identities remain unchanged and no pilot process service listener or startup hook remains
  + retrieved evidence independently verifies and states precisely what portability and performance were and were not proved

